      "text": "The probability of choosing two girls is equal to the count of pairs of two girls over the count of pairs of two people.\nWe have $\\binom{10}{2}$ pairs of two people and $\\binom{5}{2}$ pairs of two girls. Thus, the probability is $\\frac{\\binom{5}{2}}{\\binom{10}{2}}=\\frac{10}{45}=\\boxed{\\frac{2}{9}}$. The answer is \\frac{2}{9}",
